      "mergeID": "6793be8527b4f8402f9ed8b1",
      "mergedPostDetails": "For reference, I’m using an iPhone 13 Pro Max that has Bluetooth enabled but is not currently connected to any devices. \n\n(For testing sake I am alternating between using/not using AirPods during shorter play sessions, but not during this exact period in time while submitting this Canny for review.) \n\nThe current build number is (2024.4.2p2)\n\nIf I open the app by itself without having my AirPods connected, then there’s roughly a 50-65% chance that audio will NOT play over the speakers, even if all settings within the app are at 100%. This would include my phone’s volume bar as well. The only way to rectify this bug currently is to close the app and reopen it until it plays. It does, however, work without fail if I have my AirPods connected and route in game audio through Bluetooth. \n\n(Untrusted URL’s are enabled within settings, although external streams such as VRCDN and TopazChat do not currently work.)\n\nThanks for reading!",
      "mergedPostTitle": "(Occasional) No Audio without Bluetooth Headphones",
